# Focused commits (ready for main)

Keep commits small and single-purpose so any one of them can be pushed to `main` without dragging unrelated WIP.

- **One concern per commit** (e.g. FCM delivery, then separately PDF edit-mode, then separately AI prompt copy).
- Do **not** mix Android/APK, Netlify functions, CRM UI, and prompt-only edits in the same commit unless they are the same fix.
- When leftover local edits are unrelated to the current request, leave them unstaged — or commit them separately if the user wants them saved.
- Commit message: 1–2 sentences on **why**, matching recent `main` style.
- After the change is done, **commit locally** (see `local-commits-push-main.mdc`). Do not wait for “commit”.
- **Do not** `git push origin main` unless the user says “push to main” / “merge to main”.
